	(text "RS232 (U1101): fault-protected RS-232 port on UART2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "73a21676-9b4f-5214-b3fa-60a7d5841ba1")
	)
	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nAn RS-232 serial port for devices such as meters, displays and PCs. U1101 turns the ESP32 UART2 (3.3 V logic) into RS-232\nlevels (about +/-6 V) and back. Its built-in charge pump makes those voltages from 3.3 V with C1101-C1104.\nAlways on. TX and RX survive +/-70 V, so a wire to a 12/24 V supply or a short to a J1 neighbour does no damage.\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\nRS232_TXD (out): J1 pin 3: the board's transmit line (to the device's RXD); ground on J1 pin 2\nRS232_RXD (in): J1 pin 12: the board's receive line (from the device's TXD)\nUART2_TX (in): from ESP32 GPIO32 (UART2 is shared with the GPS port: one at a time)\nUART2_RX (out): to ESP32 GPIO34\n+3V3 (in): supply from the 3.3 V regulator\nGND: ground\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 265 30.65)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "69ac9e0d-8128-583c-87af-e3f482d2a955")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 119.38 55.88)
		(end 218.44 129.54)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
			(color 200 60 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "f0b1b81f-c372-57c5-a771-e2581b2aef01")
	)
	(text "keep together on the PCB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.98 56.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a9a68caa-eb12-5804-a8a4-a548e8994536")
	)
	(text "Each capacitor belongs to its own pins of U1101,\nwithin 2 mm, with short loops (GND via at the GND pads):\n  C1101 across pins 2 and 4 (C1+, C1-)\n  C1102 across pins 5 and 6 (C2+, C2-)\n  C1103 at pin 3 (V+),  C1104 at pin 7 (V-)\n  C1105 at pin 19 (VCC)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d006fbe0-798d-51c2-be87-95bd6152fbe1")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nU1101: MAX13223E RS-232 transceiver (2 drivers, 2 receivers, up to 250 kbit/s), drawn mirrored so the RS-232 pins face J1. TOUT/RIN survive +/-70 V. Always on: FORCEON and FORCEOFF to 3.3 V, EN to GND (receivers on). Channel 2 is not used: T2IN to GND; T2OUT, R2IN, R2OUT and INVALID open (X).\nC1101, C1102: 100 nF \"flying\" capacitors of the charge pump: C1101 between C1+ and C1- (pins 2, 4), C1102 between C2+ and C2- (pins 5, 6).\nC1103: 100 nF reservoir on V+ (pin 3): holds the positive supply the pump makes for the RS-232 levels.\nC1104: 1 uF reservoir on V- (pin 7): holds the negative supply.\nC1105: 100 nF decoupling for VCC (pin 19). Must sit at pin 19 on the PCB.\nNote: GND flags on the right side (T2IN, EN) are this module's GND pin, like the GND symbols."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 156 0)
		(size 155 22.45)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "64a71256-a869-5a15-85f2-d6219ad15d94")
	)
